From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] bridge: default Controller.ForceDisableB2S on

The host never opens a B2S backglass window; it shows the table's own
desktop backdrop (EM score reels, backdrop images). With the B2S plugin
linked, controller.vbs LoadController creates B2S.Server and sets B2SOn,
and B2SOn scripts hide their backdrop reels for B2S to draw scores that
go nowhere. Default upstream's 'Disable B2S' setting on, as a native
desktop setup without a B2S screen would (the vpx-js A/B harness writes
the same ForceDisableB2S = 1 for native runs).

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

diff --git a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
--- a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
+++ b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
@@ -400,6 +400,9 @@
       return 0;
    // Play in VR mode: scripts read RenderingMode = 2 and show their own room and cabinet.
    Settings::SetStandalone_RenderingModeOverride_Default(2);
+   // No B2S window exists: the host shows the table's own desktop backdrop. Hint
+   // controller.vbs off B2S, or B2SOn scripts hide their EM reels and backdrop items.
+   Settings::SetController_ForceDisableB2S_Default(true);
    g_app = new VPApp();
    g_app->InitInstance(true);
    return 0;
